.TH SLOCK 1 slock-VERSION
.SH NAME
slock \- simple screen locker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slock
[
.B \-v
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slock
is a simple screen locker. It grabs the keyboard and mouse pointer, maps a fullscreen black window, and locks the screen. 
.PP
Feedback is displayed via background color changes:
.TP
.I Black
Default state, screen is locked.
.TP
.I Blue
Typing state, characters have been entered.
.TP
.I Red
Authentication failed, input cleared.
.PP
To authenticate, type your password and press
.B Return
or
.B Enter
. To clear input, press
.B Escape
or backspace all characters.
.PP
Since this version runs without setuid privileges, it validates your password against the
.B SLOCK_PASSWORD
environment variable, falling back to a plain-text file at
.B ~/.slock_password
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
Display version information and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, non-zero on error.
